msgstr "Add the domain"

msgid "DNS server used for DNSSEC (optional)"
msgstr "DNS server used for DNSSEC (optional)"

msgid "By default, the DNS server of the GLPI server is asked. Some of them (inside Docker, for example) do not relay the DNSSEC records: DNSSEC then shows \"Unknown\". Enter the IP address of another DNS server of your organisation or of your provider to fix it."
msgstr "By default, the DNS server of the GLPI server is asked. Some of them (inside Docker, for example) do not relay the DNSSEC records: DNSSEC then shows \"Unknown\". Enter the IP address of another DNS server of your organisation or of your provider to fix it."

msgid "IP address of the DNS server"
msgstr "IP address of the DNS server"

msgid "DNS server of the GLPI server"
msgstr "DNS server of the GLPI server"

msgid "The protections in a few words"
msgstr "The protections in a few words"

msgid "List of the servers allowed to send e-mails for the domain. \"-all\" refuses all the others."
msgstr "List of the servers allowed to send e-mails for the domain. \"-all\" refuses all the others."

msgid "Signature added to each e-mail sent, checked by the receiver with a key published in the DNS under a \"selector\"."
msgstr "Signature added to each e-mail sent, checked by the receiver with a key published in the DNS under a \"selector\"."

msgid "Tells receiving servers what to do with an e-mail that fails SPF and DKIM: observe (none), put in quarantine or reject. Only quarantine and reject stop the spoofing."
msgstr "Tells receiving servers what to do with an e-mail that fails SPF and DKIM: observe (none), put in quarantine or reject. Only quarantine and reject stop the spoofing."

msgid "Require encrypted connections between mail servers, and send a report when encryption fails."
msgstr "Require encrypted connections between mail servers, and send a report when encryption fails."

msgid "Signs the DNS answers of the domain so that nobody can forge them."
msgstr "Signs the DNS answers of the domain so that nobody can forge them."

msgid "Domain added. Click \"Check now\" to read its DNS records."
msgstr "Domain added. Click \"Check now\" to read its DNS records."

msgid "Domain saved."
msgstr "Domain saved."

msgid "Domain removed from the list."
msgstr "Domain removed from the list."

msgid "DNS records read."
msgstr "DNS records read."

msgid "%d domain checked."
msgid_plural "%d domains checked."
msgstr[0] "%d domain checked."
msgstr[1] "%d domains checked."

msgid "Not saved: enter the IP address of a DNS server, for example 192.0.2.53, or leave empty."
msgstr "Not saved: enter the IP address of a DNS server, for example 192.0.2.53, or leave empty."

msgid "DNS server saved."
msgstr "DNS server saved."

msgid "Shows whether the e-mail domains of the organisation are protected against spoofing and phishing: who may send e-mails in their name (SPF), signature of the e-mails (DKIM), what receiving servers do with fake e-mails (DMARC), encryption between mail servers (MTA-STS, TLS-RPT), signature of the DNS (DNSSEC), and the expiry of the domains and of the certificate of the mail servers."
msgstr "Shows whether the e-mail domains of the organisation are protected against spoofing and phishing: who may send e-mails in their name (SPF), signature of the e-mails (DKIM), what receiving servers do with fake e-mails (DMARC), encryption between mail servers (MTA-STS, TLS-RPT), signature of the DNS (DNSSEC), and the expiry of the domains and of the certificate of the mail servers."

msgid "Enter the domains of the organisation, with the DKIM selectors given by your e-mail service and the expiry dates shown by the registrar, then click \"Check now\". The plugin only reads public DNS records: it sends no e-mail, connects to no mail server and changes nothing. Fix the gaps with your DNS host, then check again and record the result as an effectiveness test of the control."
msgstr "Enter the domains of the organisation, with the DKIM selectors given by your e-mail service and the expiry dates shown by the registrar, then click \"Check now\". The plugin only reads public DNS records: it sends no e-mail, connects to no mail server and changes nothing. Fix the gaps with your DNS host, then check again and record the result as an effectiveness test of the control."

msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.14 and A.8.21"
msgstr "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.14 and A.8.21"

msgid "Mail domains without an enforced DMARC policy (%)"
msgstr "Mail domains without an enforced DMARC policy (%)"

msgid "Mail and domain security"
msgstr "Mail and domain security"

msgid "The domain was not found in the DNS."
msgstr "The domain was not found in the DNS."

msgid "Check the spelling of the domain, or remove it if it is no longer used."
msgstr "Check the spelling of the domain, or remove it if it is no longer used."

msgid "No SPF record: anyone can send e-mails pretending to come from this domain."
msgstr "No SPF record: anyone can send e-mails pretending to come from this domain."

msgid "Publish on %s a TXT record \"v=spf1 ... -all\" listing the servers allowed to send its e-mails (for a domain that never sends e-mail: \"v=spf1 -all\")."
msgstr "Publish on %s a TXT record \"v=spf1 ... -all\" listing the servers allowed to send its e-mails (for a domain that never sends e-mail: \"v=spf1 -all\")."

msgid "Several SPF records: receiving servers ignore all of them."
msgstr "Several SPF records: receiving servers ignore all of them."

msgid "Merge them into a single TXT record starting with v=spf1."
msgstr "Merge them into a single TXT record starting with v=spf1."

msgid "SPF allows every server in the world to send for the domain (+all)."
msgstr "SPF allows every server in the world to send for the domain (+all)."

msgid "Replace +all with -all (or ~all while you check the list of servers)."
msgstr "Replace +all with -all (or ~all while you check the list of servers)."

msgid "SPF does not say what to do with the other servers (?all or no all)."
msgstr "SPF does not say what to do with the other servers (?all or no all)."

msgid "End the record with -all, or ~all while you check the list of servers."
msgstr "End the record with -all, or ~all while you check the list of servers."

msgid "SPF needs more than 10 DNS lookups: receiving servers may reject it."
msgstr "SPF needs more than 10 DNS lookups: receiving servers may reject it."

msgid "Reduce the number of include, a and mx mechanisms of the record."
msgstr "Reduce the number of include, a and mx mechanisms of the record."

msgid "SPF only marks the other servers as suspicious (~all)."
msgstr "SPF only marks the other servers as suspicious (~all)."

msgid "Move to -all once every service that sends e-mail for you is listed."
msgstr "Move to -all once every service that sends e-mail for you is listed."

msgid "No DMARC policy: receiving servers do not know what to do with fake e-mails."
msgstr "No DMARC policy: receiving servers do not know what to do with fake e-mails."

msgid "Publish a TXT record on _dmarc.%s starting with \"v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:...\", read the reports, then move to p=quarantine and p=reject."
msgstr "Publish a TXT record on _dmarc.%s starting with \"v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:...\", read the reports, then move to p=quarantine and p=reject."

msgid "The DMARC record is invalid or published several times."
msgstr "The DMARC record is invalid or published several times."

msgid "Keep a single record with p=none, p=quarantine or p=reject."
msgstr "Keep a single record with p=none, p=quarantine or p=reject."

msgid "DMARC only observes (p=none): fake e-mails are still delivered."
msgstr "DMARC only observes (p=none): fake e-mails are still delivered."

msgid "After reading the reports, move to p=quarantine, then p=reject."
msgstr "After reading the reports, move to p=quarantine, then p=reject."

msgid "DMARC applies to only part of the e-mails (pct below 100)."
msgstr "DMARC applies to only part of the e-mails (pct below 100)."

msgid "Raise pct to 100, or remove it."
msgstr "Raise pct to 100, or remove it."

msgid "DMARC sends no report (no rua address)."
msgstr "DMARC sends no report (no rua address)."

msgid "Add rua=mailto:... to receive the reports of the receiving servers."
msgstr "Add rua=mailto:... to receive the reports of the receiving servers."

msgid "A declared DKIM selector has no published key."
msgstr "A declared DKIM selector has no published key."

msgid "Check the selector name given by your e-mail service, or publish its key."
msgstr "Check the selector name given by your e-mail service, or publish its key."

msgid "A DKIM key is revoked (empty key)."
msgstr "A DKIM key is revoked (empty key)."

msgid "Remove the selector from the list if it is no longer used."
msgstr "Remove the selector from the list if it is no longer used."

msgid "No DKIM selector declared: the signature of the e-mails is not checked."
msgstr "No DKIM selector declared: the signature of the e-mails is not checked."

msgid "Enter the selectors given by your e-mail service (for example selector1 and selector2 for Microsoft 365, google for Google Workspace)."
msgstr "Enter the selectors given by your e-mail service (for example selector1 and selector2 for Microsoft 365, google for Google Workspace)."

msgid "The domain is not signed with DNSSEC: its DNS answers can be forged."
msgstr "The domain is not signed with DNSSEC: its DNS answers can be forged."

msgid "Enable DNSSEC with your registrar or DNS host."
msgstr "Enable DNSSEC with your registrar or DNS host."

msgid "DNSSEC could not be checked: the DNS server did not answer or does not relay DNSSEC records."
msgstr "DNSSEC could not be checked: the DNS server did not answer or does not relay DNSSEC records."

msgid "Check the domain again later, or choose another DNS server at the bottom of the page."
msgstr "Check the domain again later, or choose another DNS server at the bottom of the page."

msgid "No MTA-STS: encryption between mail servers is not required."
msgstr "No MTA-STS: encryption between mail servers is not required."

msgid "Publish an MTA-STS policy (record _mta-sts.%s and policy file) once your mail servers accept encrypted connections."
msgstr "Publish an MTA-STS policy (record _mta-sts.%s and policy file) once your mail servers accept encrypted connections."

msgid "No TLS-RPT: you receive no report of encryption failures."
msgstr "No TLS-RPT: you receive no report of encryption failures."

msgid "Publish a TXT record on _smtp._tls.%s: \"v=TLSRPTv1; rua=mailto:...\"."
msgstr "Publish a TXT record on _smtp._tls.%s: \"v=TLSRPTv1; rua=mailto:...\"."

